From 9c6280919f24df98d527581d6a7ad4d95e3f0d4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:33:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] MAS local: sync and shut Android down when Windows ends a
 headless session

The headless emulator has no window, so Windows does not tell it that the
session is ending (logoff, restart, shutdown). The console control handler
is not called for it either: the executable imports user32, and such a
process gets no CTRL_LOGOFF_EVENT or CTRL_SHUTDOWN_EVENT. The process is
just ended, and for the guest the power is cut. The lean window has been
handling this since ModAVD#60; this is the other half.

The safe shutdown moves out of EmulatorQtWindow into android::SafeShutdown,
as it was: sync, Android's own shutdown (svc power shutdown, init if it
refuses), a last sync and the quit when Android does not power off in time,
and the extra sync and the wait for it as the session ends. It knows nothing
of windows. What it needs comes through a Host (a way onto the owner's
thread, a timer, the quit) and Actions (the kill guard, resuming a paused
VM, registering with the adb server again), so it has unit tests now, with a
fake adb. The window keeps what is the window's: hiding itself, the title,
the shutdown block reason. Its log lines are unchanged.

The headless emulator on Windows makes a hidden top-level window on a thread
of its own and runs the same shutdown from there. WM_QUERYENDSESSION starts
it (a paused VM is resumed, the guest synced, Android asked to shut down)
and is answered with yes: a program without a visible window is not waited
for. WM_ENDSESSION makes sure a sync is running and waits up to 3 s for it,
so what was written is on disk even if Android does not get to power off.
Like the lean window it asks to be told before the default shutdown level,
so that the private adb server is still there. Not with
ANDROID_EMU_FULL_TOOLBAR=1, which keeps the emulator as it comes.

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#64

